      "text": "We start with the given equation \\(2x + 7 = 3\\). To find the value of \\(x\\), we first isolate \\(x\\) on one side of the equation. Subtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2x = -4\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-4}{2} = -2\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the equation \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) is \\(x = -2\\). This means that the variable \\(x\\) is a solution to both equations \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) and \\(bx - 10 = -2\\). Since both equations have the same solution \\(x = -2\\), we can substitute \\(x = -2\\) into the second equation \\(bx - 10 = -2\\) to find \\(b\\).\n\nSubstitute \\(x = -2\\) into the equation \\(bx - 10 = -2\\):\n\n\\[\nb(-2) - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nDistribute \\(b\\) on the left side:\n\n\\[\n-2b - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nNext, isolate the term involving \\(b\\) by adding 10 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n-2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n-2b = 8\n\\]\n\nNow, solve for \\(b\\) by dividing both sides by -2:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{-2} = -4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
